IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch3-unearned-income`

-- Tests of Part 6, Chapter 3 (regulations 65 to 74). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text of the regulation
-- and written beside the assertion; none is copied from the encoding's own output.

-- A test item of income with exactly one limb set. limb: 0 none; 1 (a) retirement pension income; 2 (b)(i) jobseeker's allowance;
-- 3 (c) foreign analogue; 4 (d) maintenance; 5 (da) foreign state retirement pension; 6 (e) student income; 8 (f) payment only;
-- 9 (f) and a substitute for universal credit; 10 (f) and for living expenses; 11 (g) Sports Council payment only; 12 (g) and for
-- living expenses; 13 (h) insurance; 14 (i) annuity; 15 (i) annuity that is retirement pension income; 16 (i) annuity disregarded
-- under reg 75; 17 (j) trust; 18 (j) trust disregarded under reg 76; 19 (j) trust disregarded under reg 75; 20 (k) yield; 21 personal
-- independence payment (not listed); 22 (l) capital treated as income; 23 (la) PPF periodic payments; 24 (m) taxable miscellaneous
-- income only; 25 (m) and retirement pension income; 26 carer support payment; 27 industrial injuries benefit; 28 widow's pension.
GIVEN limb IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Item of income considered under regulation 66`
`test item with limb` limb MEANS
    `Item of income considered under regulation 66` WITH
        `retirement pension income to which the person is entitled`  IS (limb EQUALS 1) OR (limb EQUALS 25)
        `benefit to which the person is entitled`                    IS
            BRANCH
                IF limb EQUALS 2  THEN JUST `jobseeker's allowance`
                IF limb EQUALS 21 THEN JUST `personal independence payment`
                IF limb EQUALS 26 THEN JUST `carer support payment`
                IF limb EQUALS 27 THEN JUST `industrial injuries benefit`
                IF limb EQUALS 28 THEN JUST `widow's pension`
                OTHERWISE NOTHING
        `benefit, allowance or other payment paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom and analogous to a benefit mentioned in sub-paragraph (b)`  IS limb EQUALS 3
        `payment towards the maintenance of the person by a spouse, civil partner, former spouse or former civil partner under a court order or an agreement for maintenance`  IS limb EQUALS 4
        `foreign state retirement pension`                           IS limb EQUALS 5
        `student income`                                             IS limb EQUALS 6
        `payment under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2 of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990`  IS (limb EQUALS 8) OR (limb EQUALS 9) OR (limb EQUALS 10)
        `payment is a substitute for universal credit`               IS limb EQUALS 9
        `payment is for a person's living expenses`                  IS (limb EQUALS 10) OR (limb EQUALS 12)
        `payment by a Sports Council named in section 23(2) of the National Lottery etc. Act 1993 out of sums allocated to it for distribution`  IS (limb EQUALS 11) OR (limb EQUALS 12)
        `payment received under an insurance policy to insure against the risk of losing income due to illness, accident or redundancy`  IS limb EQUALS 13
        `income from an annuity`                                     IS (limb EQUALS 14) OR (limb EQUALS 15) OR (limb EQUALS 16)
        `income from an annuity is retirement pension income`        IS limb EQUALS 15
        `income from a trust`                                        IS (limb EQUALS 17) OR (limb EQUALS 18) OR (limb EQUALS 19)
        `income from an annuity or a trust is disregarded under regulation 75`  IS (limb EQUALS 16) OR (limb EQUALS 19)
        `income from a trust is disregarded under regulation 76`     IS limb EQUALS 18
        `income treated as the yield from the person's capital by virtue of regulation 72`  IS limb EQUALS 20
        `capital treated as income by virtue of regulation 46(3) or (4)`  IS limb EQUALS 22
        `PPF periodic payments`                                      IS limb EQUALS 23
        `income taxable under Part 5 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 (miscellaneous income)`  IS (limb EQUALS 24) OR (limb EQUALS 25)

§ `Regulation 66(1) -- what is unearned income`

-- Limb (b): the benefits listed are jobseeker's allowance, ESA, carer's allowance, carer support payment, widowed mother's, widowed
-- parent's, widow's pension, maternity allowance and industrial injuries benefit. Nothing else (src:1092-1101).
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `jobseeker's allowance`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `employment and support allowance`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `carer's allowance`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `carer support payment`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `widowed mother's allowance`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `widowed parent's allowance`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `widow's pension`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `maternity allowance`
#ASSERT `reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `industrial injuries benefit`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `personal independence payment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `statutory sick pay`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1)(b) — a benefit listed in regulation 66(1)(b)` `attendance allowance`)

-- Each limb on its own makes the item unearned income; with no limb it is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 0))
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 1)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 2)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 3)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 4)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 5)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 6)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 9)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 10)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 12)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 13)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 14)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 17)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 20)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 22)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 23)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 24)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 25)
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 26)

-- Limb (f) needs the section 2 payment AND either a substitute for universal credit or living expenses (src:1106): the payment alone is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 8))
-- Limb (g): the Sports Council payment alone is not enough either; it must be for living expenses (src:1107).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 11))
-- Limb (i): an annuity that is retirement pension income is not within (i) (src:1111); it would be within (a) instead.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 15))
-- Limbs (i) and (j): income disregarded under regulation 75 or 76 is excluded (src:1111-1112).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 16))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 18))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 19))
-- A benefit that limb (b) does not list (personal independence payment) is not unearned income (src:1091-1101).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(1) — an item of income is unearned income` (`test item with limb` 21))

-- The amount that counts. Overlapping-benefit adjustment is done by the caller (the amount payable); rounding is to the penny.
GIVEN limb IS A NUMBER
      payable IS A NUMBER
      `carer's allowance amount` IS A NUMBER
      increase IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Amount of an item of income considered under regulation 66`
`test amount of an item` limb payable `carer's allowance amount` increase MEANS
    `Amount of an item of income considered under regulation 66` WITH
        item IS `test item with limb` limb
        `amount payable after any overlapping benefits adjustment` IS payable
        `amount of carer's allowance that a claimant would receive if entitled to it` IS `carer's allowance amount`
        `increase in industrial injuries benefit under section 104 or 105` IS increase

-- Jobseeker's allowance 200 counts in full (src:1092).
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 2 200 0 0) EQUALS 200
-- Carer support payment counts only up to the carer's allowance amount (src:1095): 100 against 80 gives 80; 60 against 80 gives 60.
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 26 100 80 0) EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 26 60 80 0) EQUALS 60
-- Industrial injuries benefit counts without an increase under section 104 or 105 (src:1101): 150 less 40 gives 110.
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 27 150 0 40) EQUALS 110
-- Widow's pension 90.5 counts in full.
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 28 90.5 0 0) EQUALS 90.5
-- An item that is not unearned income contributes nothing: personal independence payment 500 is not listed (src:1091-1101).
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 21 500 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- Reg 6(1) (src:172): half a penny or more counts as a penny. 100.005 rounds to 100.01; 100.004 to 100.
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 2 100.005 0 0) EQUALS 100.01
#ASSERT `reg 66(1) — the amount of an item of income that counts as unearned income` (`test amount of an item` 2 100.004 0 0) EQUALS 100

§ `Regulation 66(2) -- foreign state retirement pension and living expenses`

#ASSERT `reg 66(2)(a) — a foreign state retirement pension` (`Pension that may be a foreign state retirement pension` WITH `paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom` IS TRUE, `in the nature of social security` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(2)(a) — a foreign state retirement pension` (`Pension that may be a foreign state retirement pension` WITH `paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom` IS TRUE, `in the nature of social security` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(2)(a) — a foreign state retirement pension` (`Pension that may be a foreign state retirement pension` WITH `paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom` IS FALSE, `in the nature of social security` IS TRUE))

GIVEN food IS A BOOLEAN
      clothing IS A BOOLEAN
      housing IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A BOOLEAN
      partner IS A BOOLEAN
      child IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Cost that may be a living expense`
`test cost` food clothing housing person partner child MEANS
    `Cost that may be a living expense` WITH
        `cost of food` IS food
        `cost of ordinary clothing or footwear` IS clothing
        `cost of household fuel, rent or other housing costs (including council tax)` IS housing
        `for the person` IS person
        `for the person's partner` IS partner
        `for a child or qualifying young person for whom the person is responsible` IS child

-- Food for the person; clothing for the partner; housing for a child: each is a living expense (src:1120-1123).
#ASSERT `reg 66(2)(b) — living expenses` (`test cost` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 66(2)(b) — living expenses` (`test cost` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 66(2)(b) — living expenses` (`test cost` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A cost of the right kind for nobody the paragraph names is not; a cost of another kind (say, a holiday) is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(2)(b) — living expenses` (`test cost` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 66(2)(b) — living expenses` (`test cost` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))

§ `Regulation 67 -- retirement pension income`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Pension that may be retirement pension income`
`test pension` a b c MEANS
    `Pension that may be retirement pension income` WITH
        `retirement pension income within section 16 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 as extended by regulation 16 of the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002` IS a
        `increase in a Category A or Category B retirement pension mentioned in section 16(1)(a) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002` IS b
        `increase is payable under Part 4 of the Contributions and Benefits Act in respect of a person's partner` IS c

#ASSERT `reg 67 — retirement pension income` (`test pension` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 67 — retirement pension income` (`test pension` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 67 — retirement pension income` (`test pension` FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 67 — retirement pension income` (`test pension` FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 67 — retirement pension income` (`test pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `Regulation 68 -- student income`

-- A test course: undertaking, loan flags and the seven period facts are all parameters.
GIVEN undertaking IS A BOOLEAN
      loan IS A BOOLEAN
      postgraduate IS A BOOLEAN
      reasonable IS A BOOLEAN
      grant IS A BOOLEAN
      begins IS A BOOLEAN
      lasts IS A BOOLEAN
      second IS A BOOLEAN
      part IS A BOOLEAN
      vacationBegins IS A BOOLEAN
      withinVacation IS A BOOLEAN
      ends IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Course and assessment period considered under regulation 68`
`test course` undertaking loan postgraduate reasonable grant begins lasts second part vacationBegins withinVacation ends MEANS
    `Course and assessment period considered under regulation 68` WITH
        `undertaking a course of education, study or training` IS undertaking
        `student loan in respect of the course` IS loan
        `postgraduate loan in respect of the course` IS postgraduate
        `could acquire a student loan or a postgraduate loan by taking reasonable steps` IS reasonable
        `grant in respect of the course` IS grant
        `the course begins in the assessment period` IS begins
        `the course lasts two or more years` IS lasts
        `the second or a subsequent year of the course begins in the assessment period` IS second
        `the person undertakes the course in the assessment period or in any part of it` IS part
        `the long vacation begins in the assessment period` IS vacationBegins
        `the assessment period falls within the long vacation` IS withinVacation
        `the course ends in the assessment period` IS ends

-- (a) the assessment period in which the course begins (src:1130).
#ASSERT `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (b) a course of two or more years, the period in which the second year begins (src:1131).
#ASSERT `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A second year beginning in a course that does not last two years is not (b); with no other limb the period does not count.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (c) any other period in which, or in any part of which, the course is undertaken (src:1132).
#ASSERT `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (c)(i) excludes the period in which the long vacation begins, and a period within it (src:1133).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- (c)(ii) excludes the period in which the course ends (src:1134).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- The exclusions are limbs of (c) only: a period in which the course both begins and ends is caught by (a) (src:1130).
#ASSERT `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- No student loan, postgraduate loan or grant: no student income, even in the period the course begins (src:1129).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Not undertaking a course (regulation 13, an input): no student income.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- A grant alone, or a postgraduate loan alone, is enough to be treated as having student income.
#ASSERT `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Paragraph (5): a person who could acquire a loan by taking reasonable steps is treated as having one (src:1140).
#ASSERT `reg 68(5) — the person is treated as having a student loan or a postgraduate loan` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 68(1) — the person is treated as having student income in the assessment period` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(5) — the person is treated as having a student loan or a postgraduate loan` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- Paragraphs (2) to (4): a loan first; a grant only where there is no loan; neither: nothing to base it on (src:1135-1139).
#ASSERT `reg 68(2) to (4) — what the student income is based on` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `student income based on the amount of a loan`
#ASSERT `reg 68(2) to (4) — what the student income is based on` (`test course` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `student income based on the amount of a loan`
#ASSERT `reg 68(2) to (4) — what the student income is based on` (`test course` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `student income based on the amount of a loan`
#ASSERT `reg 68(2) to (4) — what the student income is based on` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `student income based on the amount of a loan`
#ASSERT `reg 68(2) to (4) — what the student income is based on` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `student income based on the amount of a grant`
#ASSERT `reg 68(2) to (4) — what the student income is based on` (`test course` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no loan or grant on which student income could be based`

-- Paragraph (3): 120 for rent payments plus 30 for the maintenance of another person leaves 150 of the grant; none leaves 0.
#ASSERT `reg 68(3) — the part of a grant that is not disregarded when student income is based on a loan` 120 30 EQUALS 150
#ASSERT `reg 68(3) — the part of a grant that is not disregarded when student income is based on a loan` 0 0 EQUALS 0

-- Paragraph (6): a training allowance of the kind in regulation 66(1)(f) is not student income (src:1141).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(6) — a payment counts as student income` TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 68(6) — a payment counts as student income` FALSE

-- Paragraph (7), "grant": an educational grant or award, but not a student loan and not a payment under the under-21 non-advanced scheme (src:1143).
#ASSERT `reg 68(7) — grant` (`Award that may be a grant` WITH `educational grant or award of any kind` IS TRUE, `student loan` IS FALSE, `payment under a scheme to enable persons under the age of 21 to complete courses of education or training that are not advanced education` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — grant` (`Award that may be a grant` WITH `educational grant or award of any kind` IS TRUE, `student loan` IS TRUE, `payment under a scheme to enable persons under the age of 21 to complete courses of education or training that are not advanced education` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — grant` (`Award that may be a grant` WITH `educational grant or award of any kind` IS TRUE, `student loan` IS FALSE, `payment under a scheme to enable persons under the age of 21 to complete courses of education or training that are not advanced education` IS TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — grant` (`Award that may be a grant` WITH `educational grant or award of any kind` IS FALSE, `student loan` IS FALSE, `payment under a scheme to enable persons under the age of 21 to complete courses of education or training that are not advanced education` IS FALSE))

-- Paragraph (7), "the long vacation": a period of no less than one month, in the Secretary of State's opinion the longest vacation of
-- a course of two or more years. 1 to 31 July is one month exactly; 1 to 30 July is a day short; 1 to 28 February 2027 is one month.
#ASSERT `reg 68(7) — the long vacation` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — the long vacation` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 30) TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 68(7) — the long vacation` (YearMonthDay 2027 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 28) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — the long vacation` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30) FALSE)

-- Paragraph (7), "postgraduate loan" and "student loan": both limbs are needed.
#ASSERT `reg 68(7) — postgraduate loan` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — postgraduate loan` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — postgraduate loan` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 68(7) — student loan` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — student loan` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 68(7) — student loan` FALSE TRUE)

§ `Regulations 69 and 70 -- amounts of student loans and grants`

#ASSERT `reg 69(1) — the amount of a student loan taken into account` 4000 EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT `reg 69(1) — the amount of a student loan taken into account` 4000.005 EQUALS 4000.01
-- 30 per cent. of 10,000 is 3,000; of 11,111 is 3,333.30 (src:1149).
#ASSERT `reg 69(1A) — the amount of a postgraduate loan taken into account` 10000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `reg 69(1A) — the amount of a postgraduate loan taken into account` 11111 EQUALS 3333.3

GIVEN housing IS A BOOLEAN
      awardCoversPerson IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grant counted as student income`
`test grant` housing awardCoversPerson MEANS
    `Grant counted as student income` WITH
        `whole of the grant` IS 6000
        `payment intended to meet tuition fees or examination fees` IS 2000
        `payment in respect of the person's disability` IS 500
        `payment intended to meet additional expenditure connected with term time residential study away from the person's educational establishment` IS 300
        `payment intended to meet the cost of the person maintaining a home at a place other than that at which they reside during their course` IS 400
        `an award of universal credit includes the housing costs element in respect of those costs` IS housing
        `payment intended for the maintenance of another person` IS 250
        `an award of universal credit includes an amount in respect of that other person` IS awardCoversPerson
        `payment intended to meet the cost of books and equipment` IS 100
        `payment intended to meet travel expenses incurred as a result of the person's attendance on the course` IS 50
        `payment intended to meet childcare costs` IS 80

-- 6000 less 2000, 500, 300, 400 (no housing costs element), 0 (award includes the other person), 100, 50, 80 is 2570 (src:1155-1162).
#ASSERT `reg 70 — the amount of a grant taken into account` (`test grant` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 2570
-- With the housing costs element the 400 is not excluded: 6000 - 2000 - 500 - 300 - 0 - 0 - 100 - 50 - 80 = 2970.
#ASSERT `reg 70 — the amount of a grant taken into account` (`test grant` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 2970
-- If the award includes nothing for the other person the 250 is excluded: 6000 - 2000 - 500 - 300 - 400 - 250 - 100 - 50 - 80 = 2320.
#ASSERT `reg 70 — the amount of a grant taken into account` (`test grant` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 2320
-- Both exceptions: 6000 - 2000 - 500 - 300 - 0 - 250 - 100 - 50 - 80 = 2720.
#ASSERT `reg 70 — the amount of a grant taken into account` (`test grant` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 2720

§ `Regulation 71 -- student income for an assessment period`

GIVEN basis IS A `Basis of student income`
      loan IS A NUMBER
      postgraduate IS A NUMBER
      grantPart IS A NUMBER
      grant IS A NUMBER
      hasLoan IS A BOOLEAN
      hasPostgraduate IS A BOOLEAN
      periods IS A NUMBER
      earlier IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Student income for an assessment period`
`test student income` basis loan postgraduate grantPart grant hasLoan hasPostgraduate periods earlier MEANS
    `Student income for an assessment period` WITH
        basis IS basis
        `student loan for the year of the course, or for the course if it is shorter` IS loan
        `postgraduate loan for the year of the course, or for the course if it is shorter` IS postgraduate
        `part of any grant that is not disregarded` IS grantPart
        `grant for the year of the course, or for the course if it is shorter` IS grant
        `person has a student loan` IS hasLoan
        `person has a postgraduate loan` IS hasPostgraduate
        `assessment periods in the year of the course, or in the course if it is shorter, for which the person is treated as having student income` IS periods
        `earlier months of one month each, beginning on the same day as the assessment periods, that precede the commencement of the award and fall in that year of the course or that course` IS earlier

-- Step 1: student loan 9000 plus the undisregarded grant 150 is 9150; a postgraduate loan 6000 counts 30 per cent.: 1800; a grant alone: 3000.
#ASSERT `reg 71 Step 1 — the amount of the loan or the grant` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a loan` 9000 0 150 0 TRUE FALSE 12 0) EQUALS 9150
#ASSERT `reg 71 Step 1 — the amount of the loan or the grant` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a loan` 0 6000 0 0 FALSE TRUE 12 0) EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT `reg 71 Step 1 — the amount of the loan or the grant` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a grant` 0 0 0 3000 FALSE FALSE 12 0) EQUALS 3000
-- Both a student loan and a postgraduate loan: step 1 (a) and (aa) both apply "in so far as"; the amounts add (fork F-U2): 9150 + 1800.
#ASSERT `reg 71 Step 1 — the amount of the loan or the grant` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a loan` 9000 6000 150 0 TRUE TRUE 12 0) EQUALS 10950
-- Step 2: nine periods in the year plus three earlier months is twelve.
#ASSERT `reg 71 Step 2 — the number of assessment periods` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a loan` 9000 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE 9 3) EQUALS 12
-- Steps 3 and 4: 9000 / 12 = 750; less 110 = 640.
#ASSERT `reg 71 — the student income for an assessment period` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a loan` 9000 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE 12 0) EQUALS JUST 640
-- Grant 3000 over 12 periods: 250 less 110 = 140.
#ASSERT `reg 71 — the student income for an assessment period` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a grant` 0 0 0 3000 FALSE FALSE 12 0) EQUALS JUST 140
-- 9150 over 12 = 762.5, less 110 = 652.5.
#ASSERT `reg 71 — the student income for an assessment period` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a loan` 9000 0 150 0 TRUE FALSE 12 0) EQUALS JUST 652.5
-- 1000 over 3 = 333.333..., less 110 = 223.333..., rounded under reg 6(1): 223.33.
#ASSERT `reg 71 — the student income for an assessment period` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a grant` 0 0 0 1000 FALSE FALSE 3 0) EQUALS JUST 223.33
-- The text does not floor the result at nil (fork F-U6): a grant of 600 over 12 periods is 50, less 110 is -60.
#ASSERT `reg 71 — the student income for an assessment period` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a grant` 0 0 0 600 FALSE FALSE 12 0) EQUALS JUST (0 MINUS 60)
-- No assessment period to divide by: the text does not answer, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `reg 71 — the student income for an assessment period` (`test student income` `student income based on the amount of a grant` 0 0 0 600 FALSE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 72 -- assumed yield from capital`

-- Hand-worked from "4.35 for each 250 in excess of 6,000 and 4.35 for any excess which is not a complete 250" (src:1183).
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 5999 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 6000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 6001 EQUALS 4.35
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 6250 EQUALS 4.35
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 6251 EQUALS 8.7
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 6500 EQUALS 8.7
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 6501 EQUALS 13.05
-- 16,000 is 10,000 over 6,000: forty complete 250s, 40 x 4.35 = 174.
#ASSERT `reg 72(1) — the monthly income that capital is treated as yielding` 16000 EQUALS 174
-- Paragraph (2): not where the capital is disregarded, or its actual income is taken into account as annuity or trust income.
#ASSERT `reg 72(2) — paragraph (1) applies to the capital` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 72(2) — paragraph (1) applies to the capital` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 72(2) — paragraph (1) applies to the capital` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 72(2) — paragraph (1) applies to the capital` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Paragraph (3): actual income is part of the capital from the day it is due: on the day yes, the day before no.
#ASSERT `reg 72(3) — the actual income derived from the capital is treated as part of the capital` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `reg 72(3) — the actual income derived from the capital is treated as part of the capital` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 72(3) — the actual income derived from the capital is treated as part of the capital` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 72(3) — the actual income derived from the capital is treated as part of the capital` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2))

§ `Regulation 73 -- unearned income calculated monthly`

-- 100 a week is 100 x 52 / 12 = 433.333..., rounded to 433.33; 400 four-weekly is 400 x 13 / 12 = 433.33; 300 three-monthly is 100; 1200 a year is 100.
#ASSERT `reg 73(2) — the monthly equivalent of a payment of unearned income` 100 `weekly payments` EQUALS 433.33
#ASSERT `reg 73(2) — the monthly equivalent of a payment of unearned income` 400 `four-weekly payments` EQUALS 433.33
#ASSERT `reg 73(2) — the monthly equivalent of a payment of unearned income` 300 `three-monthly payments` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `reg 73(2) — the monthly equivalent of a payment of unearned income` 1200 `annual payments` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `reg 73(2) — the monthly equivalent of a payment of unearned income` 250 `monthly payments` EQUALS 250
-- The core also has the two-weekly interval of the schedules: 200 x 26 / 12 = 433.33.
#ASSERT `reg 73(2) — the monthly equivalent of a payment of unearned income` 200 `two-weekly payments` EQUALS 433.33
-- Paragraph (2A): the formula is missing from the text: where the paragraph bites the answer is NOTHING; where it does not, the monthly amount stands.
#ASSERT `reg 73(2A) — the amount of unearned income for the assessment period` TRUE 10 300 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 73(2A) — the amount of unearned income for the assessment period` FALSE 30 300 EQUALS JUST 300
-- Paragraph (3): 1000 over a four-month cycle is 250; no cycle and no other period: three months, 900 gives 300; two months, 900 gives 450.
#ASSERT `reg 73(3) — the monthly equivalent of unearned income that fluctuates` (`Fluctuating unearned income` WITH `total unearned income received over the cycle or the period` IS 1000, `there is an identifiable cycle` IS TRUE, `duration of the identifiable cycle in months` IS 4, `other period in months that would enable the monthly equivalent to be determined more accurately` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 250
#ASSERT `reg 73(3) — the monthly equivalent of unearned income that fluctuates` (`Fluctuating unearned income` WITH `total unearned income received over the cycle or the period` IS 900, `there is an identifiable cycle` IS FALSE, `duration of the identifiable cycle in months` IS 0, `other period in months that would enable the monthly equivalent to be determined more accurately` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `reg 73(3) — the monthly equivalent of unearned income that fluctuates` (`Fluctuating unearned income` WITH `total unearned income received over the cycle or the period` IS 900, `there is an identifiable cycle` IS FALSE, `duration of the identifiable cycle in months` IS 0, `other period in months that would enable the monthly equivalent to be determined more accurately` IS JUST 2) EQUALS JUST 450
-- A cycle of no months cannot be divided by: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `reg 73(3) — the monthly equivalent of unearned income that fluctuates` (`Fluctuating unearned income` WITH `total unearned income received over the cycle or the period` IS 900, `there is an identifiable cycle` IS TRUE, `duration of the identifiable cycle in months` IS 0, `other period in months that would enable the monthly equivalent to be determined more accurately` IS NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph (4): regulation 73 does not apply to student income.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 73(4) — regulation 73 applies to the income` TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 73(4) — regulation 73 applies to the income` FALSE

